      "message": "feat(geometry): chain 2D sketch primitives into loops with stable ids and nesting\n\nAdd camcraft-geometry::sketch_chains. `chain()` joins the DXF reader's lines,\narcs and circles into closed loops and open chains within a caller join\ntolerance (default 0.01 mm), per layer, and never bridges a wider gap: such a\nchain stays open and reports its two free ends.\n\n- Curves stay analytic: a segment is the input primitive turned to the walk\n  direction, so arc centre, radius and sweep sign survive for G2/G3.\n- Closed loops are walked counterclockwise from their lowest joint, open\n  chains from their lower end; ChainId is the 128-bit FNV-1a hash of the\n  layer name and the curves in that order, quantized to 1e-6 mm.\n- Closed loops are read as outer boundaries or holes by an exact\n  crossing-number test against the arcs (even-odd, as geo2d::Region).\n- Refusals are named and per chain: duplicate primitive, segment shorter\n  than the tolerance, branching joint, self-crossing or self-touching loop,\n  zero area. Loops that cross each other keep their geometry but get\n  NestingAmbiguous instead of a role. Invalid input, bad tolerances and\n  drawings over the work budget return an error; nothing panics or hangs.\n\nAlgorithms are from published literature, named in each submodule's\nprovenance line and in docs/decisions/1861-sketch-chaining.md.\n\nFixes #1861\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
