        "date": "2026-11-16T06:10:26Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(app)!: place a DXF profile on a setup's stock - Sketch entity, ImportDxf, import_dxf MCP tool\n\nA DXF drawing is a profile that the user places on the stock of a setup.\nIt is not a model (maintainer, issue 1862, 2026-11-15).\n\n- schema: a `Sketch` component (setup + shared drawing data). The entity\n  has no facets and `model::is_model` is false for it. Its `Location` is\n  relative to the top face of the setup's stock, at the stock origin.\n- geometry: `sketch_data::SketchData` - primitives in mm, layers, source\n  units, join tolerance, chains (issue 1861) and the import summary. A\n  drawing with no unit is refused until the caller states one.\n- commands: undoable `ImportDxf(world, setup, path, options)` and\n  `MoveSketch` (X, Y, angle on the stock face). `DeleteEntity` restores a\n  profile. `MoveModel` and `DeleteSetup` refuse one by name.\n- virtual model reference (`sketch_model`): derived from the world when a\n  setup has a placed profile and the document has no part. A profile is a\n  source for the 2D milling, plasma and wire EDM kinds of its setup. A\n  kind that needs a solid, and a 3D kind in such a setup, refuse by name.\n  Generation on a profile refuses by name with what it is checked\n  against; the toolpath from chains is issue 1864.\n- project file: entity kind `sketch`, version 63. The chains are made\n  again on load. A v62 file steps up unchanged.\n- MCP: `import_dxf`, `move_dxf_profile`; `get_job` lists `profiles`, each\n  setup's `model_reference` and an operation's `checks_against`. Script:\n  `cam.importDxf`.\n\nStacked on #2106 (sketch chaining, issue 1861).\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: project files are written as version 63; older builds\nrefuse them.\n\nFixes #1862\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
